{"candidates":[{"content":"The preference for corroborated theories DEPENDS ON the biological instinct described in SRC_001. Kind: Dependence. REFUTED IF: It can be demonstrated that a rational agent devoid of evolutionary hardwiring (pure logic) would still prefer tested theories over untested ones without any appeal to survival value or psychological necessity.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"9392445bb29b107e8d0a67602ce7c39db324860f49125d03112864ecfd15b70c"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"15adc71678331108a100df74736f0137c90bcd4632e9861aadbb5b03c1583a93"}],"typicality":0.92},{"content":"The 'voluntarist decision' in SRC_003 is an ABSTRACTION of the 'evolutionary mechanism' in SRC_004, reducing the biological drive to a conscious methodological rule. Kind: Abstraction/Reduction. REFUTED IF: The voluntarist decision requires a freedom of choice that is logically incompatible with the deterministic nature of evolutionary selection pressures described in SRC_004.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"f0d217db4102565c2069cbbea590d23d19e8f6fa2fe247233af8c1957907e3f5"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"353f407b1d776de5303715a74fc26f6e762ad0db15c29200e2f10c60d0663a68"},{"role":"dependence","target":"445582b994961869eaa0c8b9e00620543302f4b6c08915d70d9b80596530a23b"}],"typicality":0.78},{"content":"SRC_002 (Implicit Induction) and SRC_005 (Verisimilitude) are in CONTRADICTION regarding the source of normative force. Kind: Contradiction. REFUTED IF: One can show that 'closeness to truth' (verisimilitude) inherently presupposes the 'uniformity of nature' (induction), thereby collapsing SRC_005 into SRC_002 and removing the contradiction.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"f4b46c0bfbb1f0b1ebb850a1505a469c6e6808782183489593b9f5409ace0d94"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"8b902069cd4a92545af148d740eca1bdcf7a116e7075a9e67f139514642b6337"},{"role":"dependence","target":"5d06de1836f586c4ff2106559e87e6dc0b307c1b85cbfb4041be8b3ecebb9840"}],"typicality":0.85},{"content":"The pragmatic 'faith' in SRC_003 INTEGRATES with the biological 'instinct' in SRC_001 to form a dual-aspect theory of scientific practice: the instinct provides the causal push, while the faith provides the normative cover. Kind: Integration. REFUTED IF: The normative cover of 'faith' is shown to be entirely redundant given the sufficiency of the biological instinct to explain behavior, rendering the integration unnecessary.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"15adc71678331108a100df74736f0137c90bcd4632e9861aadbb5b03c1583a93"},{"role":"dependence","target":"353f407b1d776de5303715a74fc26f6e762ad0db15c29200e2f10c60d0663a68"}],"typicality":0.65},{"content":"The evolutionary explanation in SRC_004 SHARED MECHANISM with the psychological instinct in SRC_001, as both rely on non-rational selection processes (biological vs. cultural) rather than logical deduction. Kind: Shared Mechanism. REFUTED IF: Cultural evolution of scientific communities operates on principles fundamentally distinct from biological natural selection, such that the 'survival' of a theory cannot be analogized to the survival of an organism.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"9392445bb29b107e8d0a67602ce7c39db324860f49125d03112864ecfd15b70c"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"15adc71678331108a100df74736f0137c90bcd4632e9861aadbb5b03c1583a93"},{"role":"dependence","target":"445582b994961869eaa0c8b9e00620543302f4b6c08915d70d9b80596530a23b"}],"typicality":0.71},{"content":"SRC_005's claim of rational methodological choice INHERITS the burden of proof from SRC_002's accusation of smuggled induction; if SRC_002 holds, SRC_005's 'rationality' is merely disguised irrationality. Kind: Inheritance (of burden). REFUTED IF: Verisimilitude can be formally defined and measured without any reference to the probability of future success, thus severing the link to inductive assumptions.","evidence_refs":[{"block":"f0d217db4102565c2069cbbea590d23d19e8f6fa2fe247233af8c1957907e3f5"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","t